==============================================================================
L4  cubic analogue of the Zudilin construction (exact, tiny n)
==============================================================================
R(t) = sum_s c_s rho^(3ts(t+s)) vanishing at t = 0..n-1 (c = kernel of the n x (n+1) matrix);
Lambda = sum_s c_s rho^(-s^3) (X - S_(s-1)) = p X - r = sum_{t>=n} R(t) rho^(t^3).
 n | v2(P X - R) | log2 max(|P|,|R|) | exponent v2/log2H | (Liouville K=n: v2/log2H)
 1 |          20 |              14.3 |            1.4021 | 5.5796
 2 |         220 |             285.4 |            0.7709 | 2.3645
 3 |         840 |            1654.9 |            0.5076 | 1.6614
 4 |        2120 |            5007.0 |            0.4234 | 1.3691
 5 |        4300 |           11352.0 |            0.3788 | 1.2113
 6 |        7620 |           23160.8 |            0.3290 | 1.1132
The kernel coefficients c_s carry the full tropical spread of rho^(3ts(t+s)); the construction
is worse than the partial sums at every n (no q-binomial cancellation exists for f(t,s) = ts(t+s)).

