==============================================================================
L7  repetition profile of swap words at block level: squares, floor(k^(3/2)), cubes
==============================================================================
LPF(j) = max_{a<j} LCE(a,j) of the swap indicator (block level; letters = 10 x blocks up to O(1)).
Two sources: (i) inside one gap (period 1 block): LPF >= distance to the next swap;
(ii) runs of equal consecutive gaps (matched swap patterns), extended by one partial gap.
Dio(w) - 1 = limsup LPF(j)/j; the table gives max LPF(j)/j over dyadic ranges of j.
  square  (blocks < 4e+06): 2^6:0.246 2^7:0.166 2^8:0.125 2^9:0.087 2^10:0.062 2^11:0.043 2^12:0.031 2^13:0.022 2^14:0.016 2^15:0.011 2^16:0.008 2^17:0.006 2^18:0.004 2^19:0.003 2^20:0.002 2^21:0.001
          fitted decay over the last dyadic ranges: LPF(j)/j ~ j^(-0.50)
  k32     (blocks < 4e+06): 2^6:0.393 2^7:0.318 2^8:0.227 2^9:0.160 2^10:0.125 2^11:0.095 2^12:0.061 2^13:0.044 2^14:0.036 2^15:0.024 2^16:0.017 2^17:0.012 2^18:0.009 2^19:0.006 2^20:0.005 2^21:0.003
