  cube    (blocks < 4e+09): 2^6:0.923 2^7:0.581 2^8:0.488 2^9:0.421 2^10:0.297 2^11:0.248 2^12:0.199 2^13:0.150 2^14:0.120 2^15:0.097 2^16:0.075 2^17:0.060 2^18:0.048 2^19:0.037 2^20:0.030 2^21:0.024 2^22:0.019 2^23:0.015 2^24:0.012 2^25:0.009 2^26:0.007 2^27:0.006 2^28:0.005 2^29:0.004 2^30:0.003 2^31:0.002
          fitted decay over the last dyadic ranges: LPF(j)/j ~ j^(-0.33)
All three profiles decay to 0: Dio = 1 for each, so Theorem D reaches none of them;
floor(k^(3/2)) is no easier than Y3 by this measure.

