Reading: ratio < 1 by a fixed factor on a sequence of N = an approximation beating Dirichlet
(irrationality exponent > 2). The lacunary controls show the detector works: sum 2^(3^k) dips
to 2/3 at N = 3^(k+1) (Hadamard gaps) and the unit cubic control sum 2^(k^3) dips only by
O(1/k) (its partial sums have exponent (k+1)^3/k^3).

